{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795108864806385039,"compiled_state":{"alias":"eatable-gauze-moth","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8c0d3d0d9bcb0e08bdcff3d898ea8c3e996abfeeee7d481ab296a8fe78055e76","event_uuid":"1c226917-ffbd-4090-badd-24aced2c4306","position":{"commit_sha":"16e5da5d13f18256aac0e47ec57dcdca4700f02e","position":"1795108864806385038-1c226917-ffbd-4090-badd-24aced2c4306"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795108864806385038,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Observation\n\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py::test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run` failed in `sweep (windows)` job 135688612206 (run 44560626779, main at 91322a91e9ed31b0523451b678cf2b3a40cdff8b): `AssertionError: run_ensures must precede build_server().run()`, with `order == ['run']`. It passed in the 3 previous Windows sweeps (jobs 135490319213, 135569438854, 135597358757). That makes it intermittent.\n\nSince 5029b61749d (\"Run MCP boot ensure sweep after listen\"), `mcp_server.main()` starts the boot sweep on a background thread (`start_startup_store_sweep`, `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:403`) and then calls `run_mcp`. The test stubs `build_server().run` and asserts the order `['ensures', 'run']`, which only holds if the thread wins the race. An earlier order-dependence bug on this test, solid-velour-lynx (de95-1594-1056-436e), is closed. Its assertion message, `got ['run']`, matches this failure.\n\n## Not established\n\n- Whether the test's stub `run` path goes through `run_mcp`, which waits on the gauge, or bypasses it.\n- Why it reproduces only intermittently.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The ordering the test asserts is either guaranteed by the code under test or replaced by an assertion that matches the async contract (for example, the sweep has completed before shutdown). The root cause is recorded with evidence.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes, and a `sweep (windows)` job on main after the fix does not list this test among its failures.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","flaky"],"ticket_id":"a5be-a825-30ea-4f09","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run races the background boot sweep thread (Windows sweep)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1c226917-ffbd-4090-badd-24aced2c4306"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795108864806385039,"uuid":"87503355-de8e-4882-8730-bfd20390b18a"}